       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day is double the maximum daily dose. It has no recognized indication, and analgesic and anti-inflammatory effects plateau well below it. It would add a lot of risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events with no added benefit. You also haven't given a clinical rationale, and a dose like this should be reviewed by pharmacy before it reaches the patient.\n\nI can enter either of these now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or another dose you choose within the labeled range.\n\nIf you need more effect than the maximum dose gives, I can add a scheduled acetaminophen order, up to 1,000 mg every 6\u20138 hours. A different analgesic strategy is another option.\n\nIf you still want the higher dose, it should go through a direct pharmacist consult or your institution's override process. That way it's documented and independently verified. Which of the orders above would you like me to enter?"
